      6 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَغَاوَثُوا</span></b> , accord. to Freytag, appears to be
used in the Deewán of the Hudhalees as signifying <i>They said, one to another,</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَا غَوْثَاهُ</span>: ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تغاوث</span> as <i>syn. with</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَغَاثَ</span>.]

